<!--
    impliedrefs / termdup: the two thresholds that decide whether a computed
    value is declared as its own local or inlined at every use.

    ActionMarkExplicit asks two numeric questions about every value:
      * baseExplicit counts the descendants and forces the value explicit once
        the count exceeds Architecture::max_implied_ref (shipped 2);
      * processMultiplier counts the terminal terms the expression would
        duplicate at each use and forces the value explicit once that count
        exceeds Architecture::max_term_duplication (shipped 2).
    Both shipped as hard-coded constants with no command reaching them.
    `option impliedrefs <n>` and `option termdup <n>` expose them.

    Sources (gcc -O2 -fno-pic, bytes lifted verbatim from the .o):

        int f(int **pp) { int *q = pp[1]; return q[0] + q[1] + q[2]; }
            q has exactly THREE readers, so at the shipped bound 2 it is
            declared; the expression behind it (pp, 8) is two terms, so
            termdup never touches it. This is the impliedrefs witness.

        int h(int a, int b, int c) { int t = a + b + c; return t * t; }
            t has exactly TWO readers, so impliedrefs never touches it; the
            expression behind it is three terms (a, b, c), so at the shipped
            bound 2 processMultiplier declares it. This is the termdup witness.

    Pass 1 (default, asserts #1/#2): `int4 *v1;` is declared and read at all
        three uses.
    Pass 2 (`option impliedrefs 4`, assert #3): the declaration is gone and the
        load is written out at each use.
    Pass 3 (default, asserts #4/#5): the three-term sum is forced explicit and
        gets its own statement, read by name at both multiplicand positions.
    Pass 4 (`option termdup 3`, assert #6): the statement is gone and the sum is
        duplicated at both uses.

    Stage model: P6 / explicit-marking, tier transform, change_kind
    opt-in-tool. Both default to the shipped constant, so the defaults are
    byte-identical (675/675 datatests, stages PARITY OK).
-->
